{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Accounting review}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Accounting_review}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Access Level Privilege}
\fs36 Accounting review
\par \fs24 This dialog is access from the \ul Accounting\plain\fs24 {\v User_Accounting} menu
\par On initial entry this dialog lists all session records sorted in date order. Duration is in Hours:Minutes
\par 
\par Session records m{\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Owner data dialog}
ay be displayed in Date or Username order
\par 
\par To restrict records by date enter dates (e.g. 18-mar-1988) in either/both of the \b From \plain\fs24 and \b To\plain\fs24  boxes and click the \{bmc bm0.bmp\}
\par 
\par To restrict sessions by Username select one of
\par \b All Users\plain\fs24 .
\par \b Username \plain\fs24 select Username required 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Owner \plain\fs24 select owner required
\par 
\par Account summary information may be displayed by selecting \b Accounts
\par \plain\fs24 
\par Information displayed may be printed on the default printer by selecting the \b Print\plain\fs24  menu item.
\par 
\par The following may be copied to the clipboard
\par Data\tab \tab The data displayed in numerical form
\par Heading\tab Column Headings
\par Owner\tab \tab The Owner information
\par 
\par This information is suitable for pasting into an Excel spreadsheet.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Activating/Deactivating user accounting}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Activating_Deactivating_user_accounting}
\pard \fs36 Activating/Deactivating user accounting
\par \fs24 This function is accessed from the \uldb Accounting\plain\fs24 {\v User_Accounting} menu.
\par The menu item \b Active \plain\fs24 is checked if the accounting function is in operation.
\par Selecting this item will toggle the accounting on/off.
\par When the accounting state is changed a \ul session record\plain\fs24 {\v Session_data} will be made to record the event.
\par \page
