{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Administrator_restrictions}
\pard \fs36 Administrator restrictions
\par \fs24 The administrator may not:
\par 
\par Edit User profiles at a higher level in the hierarchy
\par Grant Calibration priviledge
\par Perform functions assigned to higher levels
\par 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Calibration Privilege}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Calibration_Privilege}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Activating/Deactivating user accounting}
\fs36 Calibration Privilege
\par \fs24 
\par This privilege permits access to the SEM Calibration functions and parameters.
\par 
\par The privilege may only be granted by a User at the Service level of the \ul hierarchy\plain\fs24 {\v Access_Hierarchy} or greater.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Change Password}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Change_Password}
\pard \fs36 Change Password Form
\par \fs24 
\par This form is used to change the password in a \ul User Profile\plain\fs24 {\v User_Profile} and is accessed from the \ul Edit User profile\plain\fs24 {\v Edit_User_Profile_Form} form.
\par 
\par Enter the new password in both the \b New Password\plain\fs24  and \b verify\plain\fs24  boxes and click OK.
\par 
\par If changing the System password ensure that you record it in a safe place.
\par 
\par \fs32 If you forget your System password a chargeable Service visit will be required.
\par \fs24 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Compact Accounting Database}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Compact_Accounting_Database}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Administrator Main Form}
\fs36 Compact Accounting Database
\par \fs24 This function is part of \uldb User Accounting\plain\fs24 {\v User_Accounting}
\par 
\par As you change data in a database, the database file can become fragmented and use more disk space than is necessary.
\par Periodically, you can use the Compact Database function to defragment the database file. 
\par The compacted database is usually smaller and often runs faster. 
\par 
\par Before the Database is compacted it is copied to a .BAK file, which will overwrite any existing backup file.
\par 
\par Should the Compact fail for any reason you may delete the new .MDB file and rename the .BAK file to .MDB
\par \pard 
\par See also \ul Repair Accounting Database\plain\fs24 {\v Repair_Accounting_Database}
\par \page
