\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Detector Configuration}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Detector_Configuration}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Configuration Functions}
\fs36 Detector Configuration
\par \fs24 The detector Configuration is performed using the \b Detectors\plain\fs24  tab of the \ul Configuration Form\plain\fs24 {\v Configuration_Functions}.
\par 
\par Select the Detector required in the Upper Left Combo Box
\par 
\par If the selected detector is an auxiliary detector (i.e. not predefined) enter it's identity in the adjacent text box and select the type of signal it provides.
\par 
\par Select the channel identity into which the detector is plugged.
\par 
\par 
\par Repeat for any other detectors
\par 
\par A RED  message will be displayed at the bottom of the form indicating any problems with the configuration
\par \pard 
\par When configuration is complete press \b Save Settings\plain\fs24  to action the configuration
\par \page
