{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Edit User Profile}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Edit_User_Profile}
\pard \fs36 Edit User Profile
\par \fs24 
\par A \ul User profile\plain\fs24 {\v User_Profile} may be edited in two ways from the Administrator main Window
\par :
\par Select the User Profile to be edited (click on the item in the list of profiles) and select menu item \b Users\plain\fs24  - \b Edit\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par Double click the User profile in the list of profiles
\par 
\par The \uldb User Profile\plain\fs24 {\v Edit_User_Profile_Form} form will be displayed
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Edit User Profile Form}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Edit_User_Profile_Form}
\pard \fs36 Edit User Profile Form
\par \fs24 This form is used to Edit an existing \ul User Profile\plain\fs24 {\v User_Profile} 
\par 
\par UserName may not be changed.
\par Password. Select \uldb Change Password\plain\fs24 {\v Change_Password} if required.
\par Click on the \uldb User Directory\plain\fs24 {\v Directory_Selection_Form} to change 
\par Click on the \uldb Image Directory\plain\fs24 {\v Image_Directory_Selection_Form} to change
\par Select \ul User Level permissions\plain\fs24 {\v 2Z0A0ZB}
\par Select \ul User\plain\fs24 {\v User_Directory_Change_Privilege}/\ul Image\plain\fs24 {\v Image_Directory_Change_Privilege} Directory Change permissions
\par Select Privileges (\ul Calibration\plain\fs24 {\v Calibration_Privilege}, \ul Supervisor\plain\fs24 {\v 3CNN77}, \ul Stage Initialise\plain\fs24 {\v Stage_Initialise_Privilege},   \ul Unlock Icons\plain\fs24 {\v Unlock_Toolbar_Icon_privilege}).
\par \pard 
\par Note: Ensure that the User who's profile is being edited is not logged on to the SEM if you wish to alter the user's User or Image Directory. This is because when logging off the current User and Image directories are written to the database which would overwrite your changes. 
\par \page
