{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Installing Licences from disk}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Installing_Licences_from_disk}
\pard \fs36 Installing Licences from disk
\par \fs24 Licences may be installed from a licence file on disk as follows
\par 
\par Insert Licence disk in Drive A:
\par On the \ul Licence Administration Form\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_Administration_Form} press \b Install From Disk\plain\fs24 
\par Select the \ul licence file\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_File}. 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Licence Administration Form}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Licence_Administration_Form}
\pard \fs36 Licence Administration Form
\par \fs24 This form is accessed from the Administrator Main Window using the \b Licences\plain\fs24  menu item
\par 
\par The Leo-32 Server is started if not already running. This is done so that the Server may perform the \ul Licence validation\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_validation}.
\par 
\par The current Server licence set is displayed in the list box.(Exception - \ul Restore Licences\plain\fs24 {\v Restore_Licences})
\par 
\par Licences which are standard are marked with an asterisk (*)
\par Disabled Licences are marked with an X
\par 
\par Licences in the list may be \ul edited\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_Editing}
\par \pard 
\par \ul Installing Licences from disk\plain\fs24 {\v Installing_Licences_from_disk}
\par 
\par \ul Restore Licences\plain\fs24 {\v Restore_Licences}
\par 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Licence Editing}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Licence_Editing}
\pard \fs36 Licence Editing
\par \fs24 An Installed licence may be edited (i.e. temporarily disabled or re-enabled) in the \ul Licence Administration Form\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_Administration_Form} by selecting the licence (click on the required licence to highlight it) and press the Enable/Disable Licence button.
\par 
\par A disabled licence is marked with an X
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Licence File}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Licence_File}
\pard \fs36 Licence File
\par \fs24 A licence file is an encrypted file containing licences for a specific serial numbered SEM
\par 
\par The licence file has extension \b .LIC\plain\fs24 , the file name is typically an order number (e.g. MW12345.LIC)
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Licence administration}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Licence_administration}
\pard \fs36 Licence administration
\par \fs24 
\par Licences are used to enable specific functionality in the software.
\par 
\par Some licences are provided as standard with a specific model of SEM, others are purchased as options.
\par 
\par When the SEM is delivered the Standard and purchased licences are already installed.
\par 
\par For security the licences provided are also supplied on a floppy disk for reinstallation if required.
\par 
\par Additional licences purchased will be supplied on floppy disk for installation on the SEM.
\par \pard 
\par \uldb Licence Administration Form\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_Administration_Form}
\par \ul Licence Validation\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_validation}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Licence validation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Licence_validation}
\pard \fs36 Licence validation
\par \fs24 The installed licences are held in the leo database as a master copy.
\par Licences are valid only for a specific instrument Serial Number.
\par On Server Start up Serial Number checks are performed and if successful the licences are transferred to the Server which is their normal working location.
\par If the validation checks fail a failure message is displayed in the Server Window and the Server does not receive any licences, even those which are standard of the specific model of SEM.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Log On Form}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Log_On_Form}
\pard \fs36 Log On Form
\par \fs24 
\par On starting the Leo-32 Administrator you are requested to enter a UserName and password. 
\par 
\par Only by entering a valid UserName and password will you be able to proceed beyond this point.
\par 
\par Both UserName and password are case insensitive.
\par 
\par On initial installation of the Leo-32 Software the SEM Supervisor should log on as SYSTEM with a blank password and change the password to a suitable string.
\par This password will take effect on the next log on.
\par 
\par \fs32 Please record this password in a safe place
\par \pard If you forget your password a chargeable Service visit will be required.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} New User Profile Form}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} User_Profile_Form}
\pard \fs36 New User Profile Form
\par \fs24 This form is used to create a new \ul User Profile\plain\fs24 {\v User_Profile} 
\par 
\par Enter Username - this must be unique
\par The password will default to the Username
\par Click on the \uldb User Directory\plain\fs24 {\v Directory_Selection_Form} to define 
\par Click on the \uldb Image Directory\plain\fs24 {\v Image_Directory_Selection_Form} to define
\par Select \ul User Level permissions\plain\fs24 {\v 2Z0A0ZB}
\par Select \ul User\plain\fs24 {\v User_Directory_Change_Privilege}/\ul Image\plain\fs24 {\v Image_Directory_Change_Privilege} Directory Change permissions
\par Select Privileges (\ul Calibration\plain\fs24 {\v Calibration_Privilege}, \ul Supervisor\plain\fs24 {\v 3CNN77}, \ul Stage Initialise\plain\fs24 {\v LJGPJG}  \ul Unlock Icons\plain\fs24 {\v Unlock_Toolbar_Icon_privilege}).
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Overview}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Overview}
\pard \fs36 Overview
\par \fs24 The Leo-32 Administrator provides controlled access to the Leo-32 \ul Database\plain\fs24 {\v Database_location}  which contains critical system information. It is essential that the database be regularly backed up to a secure destination.
\par 
\par There is a \ul hierarchy\plain\fs24 {\v Access_Hierarchy} of access to the database, the functions available being controlled by the position of the Username in the hierarchy.
\par 
\par The following administrative functions are provided:
\par 
\par \ul User profile Functions\plain\fs24 {\v User_profile_Functions}
\par \ul Licence administration\plain\fs24 {\v Licence_administration}
\par \pard\tx355 \ul \ul System Configuration\plain\fs24 {\v Configuration_Functions}
\par Service Functions\tab [Not available for Customer use]
\par Factory Functions\tab [Not available for Customer use]
\par 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Owner Relation}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Owner_Relation}
\pard\tx355 \fs36 Owner Relation
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 The Owner Relation record for the \uldb User Accounting database\plain\fs24 {\v User_Accounting_database} contains
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b OwnerID\tab \plain\fs24 see \ul Owner Data\plain\fs24 {\v Owner_information}
