{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Protected Z}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Protected_Z}
\pard \fs36 Protected Z
\par \fs24 
\par This SEM parameter controls the behaviour of the stage when a multi axis move is performed (e.g. Go To a position label).
\par 
\par \b Parameter not Set\plain\fs24 .
\par All relevent axis move simultaneously to the desired position.
\par Backlash correction performed if required.
\par 
\par \b Parameter Set\plain\fs24 
\par The move to the desired position is performed in phases to minimise the risk of collision. 
\par 
\par 
\par The movement sequence is:
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par If the desired Z is lower than the current Z then this axis is moved to the desired position.
\par If the desired Tilt is lower than the current Tilt then this axis is moved to the desired position
\par The X,Y,R,M axes are moved simultaneously to their desired positions
\par If The desired Tilt position is not yet achieved move Tilt to the desired position
\par If the desired Z position is not yet achieved move Z to the desired position.
\par 
\par 
\par This \b Protected Z\plain\fs24  parameter may only be changed with \ul Supervisor Privilege\plain\fs24 {\v 3CNN77}.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Repair Accounting Database}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Repair_Accounting_Database}
\pard\tx355 \fs36 Repair Accounting Database
\par \pard\tx355 \fs24 This function is part of \uldb User Accounting\plain\fs24 {\v User_Accounting}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 This function attempts to repair a database that was marked as possibly corrupt by an incomplete write operation. This can occur if an application using the  database is closed unexpectedly because of a power outage or computer hardware problem. 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 This function also attempts to validate all system tables and all indexes. Any data that can't be repaired is discarded. If the database can't be repaired, an error occurs.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 When you attempt to open or compact a corrupted database, an error usually occurs. In some situations, however, a corrupted database may not be detected, and no error occurs. It's a good idea to use this function if the database behaves unpredictably.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Note   After repairing a database, it's also a good idea to \ul compact\plain\fs24 {\v Compact_Accounting_Database} it  to defragment the file and to recover disk space.
\par \page
