\par The control interface of the SEM comprises Commands, Analogue parameters and Digital parameters.
\par The total items  number many hundreds, hence when selecting parameters from a list (for display in the status window, parameters for annotation,  parameters in macros, etc) it is necessary to have a method of reducing the parameters listed.
\par 
\par Every item is assigned a \ul User Category\plain\fs24 {\v User_Category}
\par A user may select (part of SEM User Preferences) the \ul level\plain\fs24 {\v User_level} at which he wishes to operate.
\par \pard 
\par This choice may be restricted in the \ul User Profile\plain\fs24 {\v User_Profile}
\par 
\par '\b Any Level' Checked\plain\fs24 
\par User has unrestricted choice of level
\par 
\par '\b Any Level' Unchecked\plain\fs24 
